  "description": "Second diagnostic scenario, NOT a permanent template. The first diagnostic (diagnostic_05_no_orbit_maintenance.json, no force effector at all) ran the full 7 days with no crash -- proving the crash is tied to a force effector being active on follower-1, not core gravity/integrator setup.\n\nThis one isolates WHICH PART of that: identical orbits/duration/rate/integrator/gravity to 05_formation_flying_phasing.json, but follower-1 has ONLY constant_thrust configured (a small constant 0.05N prograde burn, same magnitude used elsewhere in template 05) -- no station_keeping, no phasing_keeping, none of their state machines, altitude smoothing, thrust arbitration, or eclipse gating. It still shares the exact same propellant/mass-bookkeeping pattern (engine.propellant_bookkeeping.apply_propellant_burn, writing scObject.hub.mHub every tick) all three orbit_maintenance controllers use.\n\nIf this crashes the same way, the trigger is in the shared force-effector/mass-bookkeeping mechanism itself (used by all three controllers), not in station_keeping/phasing_keeping's own extra logic. If it does NOT crash, that points specifically at StationKeepingController/PhasingKeepingController's own logic (state machine, altitude smoothing, thrust arbitration, or eclipse gating) as the actual trigger.",
  "schema_version": 1
